# Task 5 – Complete Pharmacovigilance Assessment

## Objective

To perform a complete pharmacovigilance assessment of a simulated Individual Case Safety Report (ICSR), including adverse drug reaction (ADR) identification, case processing, seriousness and severity assessment, causality assessment, dechallenge evaluation, reporting requirements, and final drug safety assessment.

This task simulates the role of a Drug Safety Associate responsible for reviewing an adverse event report and determining the appropriate pharmacovigilance assessment.

> **Note:** The patient case presented in this assignment is a simulated educational case created for the purpose of this pharmacovigilance internship assignment. It does not represent a real patient or real-world individual case safety report.

