# 1. Case Study

## Case Title

**Amoxicillin-Clavulanate Associated Generalized Urticaria and Angioedema in an Adult Patient**

## Case Overview

A 32-year-old female patient was prescribed amoxicillin-clavulanate for the treatment of an acute bacterial respiratory tract infection.

The patient received amoxicillin-clavulanate 625 mg orally three times daily. Approximately two hours after taking the third dose on Day 2 of treatment, the patient developed generalized itching followed by widespread urticarial skin lesions.

Within approximately 30 minutes, the patient developed swelling of the lips and mild facial swelling. She also reported a sensation of throat tightness but did not lose consciousness.

The medication was immediately discontinued and the patient was taken to the emergency department.

She was treated with an antihistamine, corticosteroid and supportive management. Her symptoms improved substantially within several hours and the patient was discharged after observation.

The suspected medicine was not restarted.

