# 18. ADR Reporting Assessment

Because this case involves a serious suspected ADR, it should be documented and reported through the appropriate pharmacovigilance pathway.

For an Indian pharmacovigilance scenario, the suspected ADR can be documented using the **PvPI Suspected Adverse Drug Reaction Reporting Form** and submitted to an appropriate ADR Monitoring Centre or the National Coordination Centre of PvPI. The Indian Pharmacopoeia Commission also provides ADR reporting tools and supports reporting by healthcare professionals.

### Reporting Information

**Reporting pathway:**

Healthcare Professional
↓
Suspected ADR Reporting Form
↓
ADR Monitoring Centre / NCC-PvPI
↓
Causality Assessment and Pharmacovigilance Evaluation
↓
Safety Database / Further Signal Assessment

PvPI states that submitted reports are handled confidentially and that causality assessment is carried out at ADR Monitoring Centres using the WHO-UMC scale.

